        "heading": "How is Aerovironment’s federal business performing?",
        "body": "Aerovironment has $511M in obligations in FY2026 to date and obligations are up 3.0% year over year. Aerovironment has 66 awards so far in the fiscal year, with an average award size of $7.7M. Aerovironment’s FY26 total follows year-by-year growth from $10.4M in FY21, $58.9M in FY22, $321M in FY23, $215M in FY24, and $496M in FY25."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are Aerovironment’s top government customers and markets?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is Aerovironment’s largest buyer and obligated $510M in FY2026 to date. Aerovironment’s top market is Aircraft Manufacturing with $489M in obligations, followed by Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) with $21.9M. Aerovironment also has obligations from the Department of Transportation and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration, which obligated $575K and $111K respectively."
      }
